    "evidence_text": "The proposed dataset, consisting of 1900 collected dialogs, allows simulation of an interactive gaining of denotations and questions explanations from users which can be used for the interactive learning.\n\nIntroduction\tNowadays, dialog systems are usually designed for a single domain  .\n\nHowever, the well-defined structure of the database of a typical dialog system comes with a high cost of extending it as every piece of new information has to fit\n\nA dialog system based on knowledge bases offers many advantages.\n\nFrom the point of view of dialog systems providing general information from a knowledge base, the most limiting factor is that a large portion of the questions is understood poorly.\n\nThe dialog variants we are considering for interactive learning differ only in presence of several parts of the dialog.\n\nFor evaluation purposes we need information whether dialog contains the answer\n\nDataset Properties\tWe collected the dataset with 1900 dialogs and 8533 turns.\n\n351 of all collected dialogs contain correct answer provided by users and 702 dialogs have incorrect answer.\n\nIn the remaining 847 dialogs users did not want to answer the question.\n\nThe collected dialogs also contain 1828 paraphrases and 1539 explanations for 1870 questions.\n\nExample\n\ndialog models.",
